Q7. Why are there two conditions inside the inner while?
read < chars.size() &&
chars[read] == currentChar
The first condition prevents accessing memory outside the array.
The second condition checks whether we're still in the same group.
Both conditions are necessary.
If we removed the first condition,
chars[read]
could access an invalid index when read == chars.size().
