Q16. Why is the time complexity O(n)?
Every character is processed exactly once by the read pointer.
The write pointer only moves forward.
Neither pointer moves backward.
Therefore,
O(n)
-------------------------------------------------------------

Q17. Why isn't the nested while loop O(n²)?
This is one of the most common interview questions.
Although there is a while loop inside another while loop,
the inner loop does not restart from the beginning.
Example
a a a b b c
read moves
0
↓
1
↓
2
↓
3
↓
4
↓
5
↓
6
Each character is visited exactly once.
Total work
n
not
n × n
This pattern is called the two-pointer technique or an amortized linear scan.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

